==Enemy==
Diabrollow is a peon that behaves similarly to Brollow, having somewhat high damage, full backswing, close range and many knockbacks with decent health. Its 100% chance for both knockback and level 3 [[Wave Attack|Mini-Waves]] shouldn't be discounted either, able to extend its reach all the way up to 867.5.

==Strategy==
The sheer damage, Mini-Wave, and guaranteed knockback all serve to make Diabrollow an annoying pusher, especially when 15 knockbacks allow for even a weak attack to activate a troublesome rebound mechanic. However, a 100% Diabrollow only has 60,000 HP and can thus be one-shot by several damage-dealers. The sooner an attacker such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can reach and attack it, the better. The problem is that Diabrollow is usually spammed in stages that it appears in, and the repeated knockbacks from its Mini-Waves can cause you to rapidly lose ground, allowing the other threats in the stage to push hard. Their constant knockbacks may also keep interrupting the attack animations of nukers like [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], preventing them from attacking at all. If they get too numerous, a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or [[Immune to Waves|Wave-immune units]] may be required to keep them at bay.

Since Diabrollow's Mini-Waves deal very low damage (2,400 at 100% strength magnification, which isn't even enough to kill a level 45+ [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]]), you can use them to your advantage by skipping the backswings of rushers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or repositioning backline units that can be hit by it.

While the Sage type does give Diabrollow resistance to all status effects, this will rarely matter, as raw damage is more than enough to defeat it.

