==Trivia==
*Diabrollow's name is a combination of ''diabolical'', ''diablo'' (Spanish for devil) or ''diavolo'' (Italian for devil) and ''[[Brollow]]''. It may also involve ''diamond'' (referencing the gemstone it carries).
*Diabrollow's Japanese name, Tsubasatān (ツバサターン, "Tsubasaturn"), is derived from 燕 ''tsubame'' ([[wikipedia:Swallow|swallow]]), 翼 ''tsubasa'' (wing), サターン ''Satān'' (Saturn) and ''Satan''. In this context, "Saturn" does not refer to the planet, but to a [[wikipedia:Saturn (mythology)|Roman deity]] conflated with the Greek Titan [[wikipedia:Cronus|Cronus]], whose sister-wife Rhea gave him a stone that he swallowed thinking it was his sixth child, Zeus, just like how Diabrollow has a [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] stone in its beak. After Cronus was overthrown by the Olympians, he was banished to [[wikipedia:Tartarus|Tartarus]], a pit of the underworld where the wicked are tormented, hence why Diabrollow is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy.
**In Japan, the Roman god Saturn is normally called サトゥルヌス ''Saturunusu'' (Saturnus), but Saturn's English name transliterated into Japanese is サターン ''Satān''.
**Diabrollow's description references how some birds are attracted to and collect shiny objects. This behavior is often misattributed to crows, which relates to Cronus because [[wikipedia:Robert Graves|Robert Graves]] posited that Cronus could mean "crow", like the Latin ''cornix'' and the Greek ''corōne''.
**Diabrollow is greedy for valuables, while Cronus was greedy for power.
**Diabrollow appears to have two small, thin horns on its head, which may reference the 19th-century theory tracing Cronus' name to the Semitic root ''qrn'', meaning "horn".
**Diabrollow's Sage type may refer to how [[wikipedia:Plato|Plato]] etymologized "Cronus" as a compound of κοῦρος (''koûros'', "youth, young man"), καθαρός (''katharós'', "pure"), and νοῦς (''noûs'', "mind, intellect"), thus meaning "he of pure intellect", as described on [https://mythopedia.com/topics/cronus Mythopedia].
**Cronus' weapon was a scythe, sickle or [[wikipedia:Harpe|harpe]], and Diabrollow's wings are shaped somewhat like the blade of a scythe. Its wings also resemble a huge, gaping maw, befitting a Titan who swallowed his children.
**Cronus is often confused with the god of time, [[wikipedia:Chronos|Chronos]], and Diabrollow appears in [[Meeting of Long and Short]], the last stage of a [[A Journey of Moments|time-themed sub-chapter]].
*Diabrollow can be seen as the antithesis of the swallow from "[[wikipedia: The Happy Prince and Other Tales|The Happy Prince]]" by [[wikipedia:Oscar Wilde|Oscar Wilde]]. In the story, a statue of a prince tells a swallow to take his possessions and give them to the poor, including a pair of sapphires from his eyes. The swallow dies in the winter, but his altruism allows him to go to Heaven alongside the prince. While Diabrollow carries a blue gem like the prince's sapphires, it is a demon defined by its greed.
*Diabrollow's black-and-blue wings may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Black saw-wing|Psalidoprocne pristoptera]]'', a species of swallow commonly known as both the black saw-wing and the blue saw-wing.
*[[Resort De La Cospa]]'s [[wikipedia:Tourist trap|tourist trap]] theme is likely a reference to Diabrollow's greed. "Cospa" in Japanese is コスパ ''kosupa'' (short for コストパフォーマンス ''kosuto pafōmansu'', [[wikipedia:Price–performance ratio|cost-performance]]).
*Diabrollow's debut stage, [[Pre-Fab Cathedral]], pairs it with [[Two Can]], another greedy bird with [[Wave Attack|Wave]]s.

